rval of 2.1 to 4.7. December accounts for 2% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 34 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,992 euros, was awarded in September 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper conduct. It could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or the need for multiple suppliers for the same service. Statistical patterns alone do not prove wrongdoing in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts across different sectors to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review the awardee A's contracts to determine if they consistently meet the same need. Examine the dates of contracts [1], [2], and [3] to assess if they were awarded in a pattern that might suggest strategic timing.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["aWZM3iMrUMMeC9GJQOEBkQ%3D%3D","XHQu2D%2BF73FeKgd8LfVV9g%3D%3D","ntO%2BcK%2BjC0kZDGvgaZEVxQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}